<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1539" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδών-ιος</span></b> , ὁ, rare
		form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄδωνις</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.756c
		</span></i>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Adj.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
				<i>of Adonis</i>:—hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδώνιον, τό</span>, <i>a statue
				of him</i> borne in the Adonia, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (sub. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέτρον</span>) a kind of <i>verse</i>, consisting of a
			dactyl and spondee, Sacerd.<i><span class="en">
				p.516
			</span></i> K. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄδωνις</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				21.60
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
